  "generated_text": "Given:\n- \\(\\angle D = 25^\\circ\\)\n- \\(\\angle E = 90^\\circ\\)\n- \\(EF = 9\\)\n\nWe need to find \\(DE\\).\n\nSince \\(\\angle E = 90^\\circ\\), triangle \\(DEF\\) is a right triangle.\n\nFirst, we use the definition of sine in a right triangle:\n\\[\n\\sin(25^\\circ) = \\frac{DE}{EF}\n\\]\n\nUsing a calculator to find \\(\\sin(25^\\circ)\\):\n\\[\n\\sin(25^\\circ) \\approx 0.4226\n\\]\n\nNow, we can set up the equation:\n\\[\n0.4226 = \\frac{DE}{9}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(DE\\):\n\\[\nDE = 0.4226 \\times 9\n\\]\n\\[\nDE \\approx 3.8034\n\\]\n\nRounding to the nearest tenth:\n\\[\nDE \\approx 3.8\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of \\(DE\\) to the nearest tenth is \\(\\boxed{3.8}\\).",
  "grade": {
